  "worked_solution": "If the amount of water in the beaker is $W$ milliliters, then the rate of change of the amount of water is $\\frac{\\text{d}W}{\\text{d}t},$ where $t$ is the time in seconds.\n\nSince $2$ milliliters of water are lost every second, the rate of change of the amount of water is given by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}W}{\\text{d}t}=-2.\n$$\n\nThe right-hand side is negative because the beaker is losing water.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
